      {
       "title": "Read off both centres and radii",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "Circle $c$ has centre $(-2, 1)$ and radius $\\sqrt{100} = 10$."
        },
        {
         "text": "Circle $s$, $(x-7)^2 + (y-13)^2 = 25$, has centre $(7, 13)$ and radius $5$."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Compare the sum of the radii with the distance between centres",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "r_1 + r_2 &= 10 + 5"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 15"
        },
        {
         "tex": "d &= \\sqrt{(7-(-2))^2 + (13-1)^2}"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= \\sqrt{9^2 + 12^2}"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= \\sqrt{81 + 144}"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= \\sqrt{225}"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= 15"
        },
        {
         "text": "The distance between the centres equals $r_1 + r_2$, so the circles touch externally."
        }
       ]
      }
