    "workedSolution": {
     "steps": [
      {
       "title": "Write the volume in terms of h and pi",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "V &= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h"
        },
        {
         "text": "Substitute $r^2 = 20h - h^2$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "V &= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(20h - h^2)h"
        },
        {
         "tex": "&= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(20h^2 - h^3)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Differentiate with respect to h",
       "lines": [
        {
         "tex": "\\frac{dV}{dh} &= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(40h - 3h^2)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Set the derivative equal to zero",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "At a maximum, $\\frac{dV}{dh} = 0$."
        },
        {
         "tex": "\\frac{1}{3}\\pi(40h - 3h^2) &= 0"
        },
        {
         "tex": "40h - 3h^2 &= 0"
        },
        {
         "tex": "h(40 - 3h) &= 0"
        },
        {
         "tex": "h = 0 \\quad &\\text{or} \\quad h = \\frac{40}{3}"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "title": "Choose the correct value",
       "lines": [
        {
         "text": "$h = 0$ gives $V = 0$, which is not a maximum. So the maximum is at $h = \\frac{40}{3}$."
        },
        {
         "text": "Check: $\\frac{d^2V}{dh^2} = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(40 - 6h)$, which at $h = \\frac{40}{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3}\\pi(-40) < 0$, so it is a maximum."
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "finalAnswer": "V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(20h^2 - h^3), \\quad h = \\frac{40}{3} \\text{ cm}"
    }
